{
  "requirement": "Under {cite}`requirements.cli.skill_structure`, the `habeas` skill MUST be the home of routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and gotchas common to every task.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The subject requires the `habeas` skill to be the single home of five topics: routing tasks to skills, `habeas status` and `habeas info`, directive and reference syntax, distributed requirements, and gotchas common to every task. The cited parent, `requirements.cli.skill_structure`, adds that each topic is stated in full in exactly one skill. `the_habeas_skill_is_home_of_routing_inspection_syntax_and_shared_gotchas` in `tests/authoring_cli.rs` is the marked test. I did not read the skill assets themselves, only the test and its helpers.\n\n**Obligations mapped to assertions**\n\n- **Routing.** The test extracts the `## Workflow` section of `habeas/SKILL.md` with `section` and asserts it contains the routing table header `| Task | Skill |`.\n- **`habeas status` and `habeas info`.** It asserts that `## Inspecting` contains both `habeas status [<selection>]` and `habeas info <selection>`.\n- **Directive syntax.** It asserts that `## Requirements, examples, and definitions` names the `{req}`, `{example}` and `{definition}` directives.\n- **Reference syntax.** It asserts that `## References` has the comment-reference rule and the fenced-reference rule.\n- **Gotchas.** It asserts that `## Gotchas` contains the reference-discovery working-directory gotcha.\n- **Distributed requirements.** It requires `references/distributed-requirements.md` to exist, using `skill_file`, which panics if the file is missing, and asserts it has the `# Distributed requirements` heading. It also requires `references/syntax-details.md` with its `## Full names in nested chapters` and `## Anchors` headings.\n- **Home, exactly one skill.** `assert_home(\"habeas\")` does two things. It asserts the `habeas` skill, with its references collapsed, contains every `home_markers(\"habeas\")` phrase. Those phrases cover the routing table, selection and glob syntax, full-name derivation, fenced references, `:::{violations}`, site queries, the `silently defines nothing` gotcha, the outer-fence gotcha, the target-directory gotcha and the install prerequisites. It also asserts that none of the other four bundled skills contains any of those phrases, so a topic restated elsewhere fails with `{other} restates habeas's …`.\n\n**Assessment**\n\nThe assertions are real: `assert_text` and `assert_home` use `assert!`. A failure of either obligation would be caught. If the section, table or phrases were missing from `habeas`, the test would fail. If another skill copied the marker text, the exclusivity loop would fail.\n\nBecause the obligation is about where documentation lives, checking phrases and sections is a reasonable way to test it. The other four skills have their own marked tests under their sibling requirements. The parent requirement's tests are out of scope here. I found no unmarked relevant test and no gap, and there are no `{fixme}` acknowledgments.",
  "references": "3e613787d62d50092286fd528020c2381ceb86235c44291883f55c4a6d9690e7",
